# Build-configuration outputs: GENERATED by build_profile.py (tools/profile_gen.py) from
# tools/profile/pll_template.v and tools/profile/z486_mister.sdc.in for the configuration the
# qsf records. The templates are the source; switching profiles must not dirty the tree.
/z486_mister.sdc
/rtl/pll.qip
/rtl/pll.v
/rtl/pll.bsf
/rtl/pll/pll_0002.v
/tests/obj_dir/
/tests/pc9821/build/
/firmware/diagnostic/*.bin
/firmware/diagnostic/*.mem
/build/*.bin
/build/*.mem
# The deployed firmware pack (runtime ROM data, never committed - it carries the
# user's BIOS/font and Yamaha's rhythm image). The build writes build/, but a pack
# copied next to the tree for inspection/deploy must not show as tree dirt either.
/pc98pack*.bin
/mister_deploy/games/**/*.bin
build_id.v
c5_pin_model_dump.txt
# Bench logs (tools/bench.py writes build/measure/)
/build/measure/
# Historical gate logs (the gate tool is no longer in the tree; kept so old runs stay ignored)
/build/gate/

# Python bytecode from the tools importing the generator
__pycache__/

# ABC's session history, written in the directory Yosys is run from
abc.history

# Quartus build scratch: 2.2-2.7 GB per tree, on real storage, never committed.
.build/

# Lane worktrees: in-repo per AGENTS.md's self-containment rule, never committed.
.worktrees/

# hwprobe: the DOS .COM binaries are built by tools/hwprobe/Makefile, not vendored
/tools/hwprobe/**/*.com

# Local scratch space (analysis, recordings, probe packs): never committed.
/scratch/

# the INT21 capture DECODES: a pure function of the tracked raw logs, so they are not
# tracked. Regenerate with: tools/decode_telemetry.py --clk-mhz=50 <raw>.log
docs/probes/int21-mister-2026-09-30/*-decoded.txt

# --- Verilator / C++ build output -------------------------------------------------------
# A build tree is never an artifact. Quartus outputs are covered above; these are the ones
# that slipped in: a Verilator obj*/ tree holds ~26 files per configuration, and a
# `git add -A` sweeps every one of them in.
obj_dir/
obj*/
*.o
*.a
*.d

# Runtime inputs: disk images and the firmware pack are the user's own dumps, not repo artifacts,
# and must never be committed (AGENTS.md, "Firmware pack (runtime inputs)").
*.img
*.vhd
pc98pack*.bin

# Guest binaries pulled out of a disk image to analyse a game: commercial data that
# must never be committed (AGENTS.md), and an analysis product of one is that same code.
# `*.EXE` is unambiguous HERE - no build or tool in this repo emits one, and a game off a DOS
# disk is always the uppercase 8.3 form (both cases are listed because nothing legitimate is
# being excluded either way) - and `*.idata` is undiet.py's decompressed output, i.e. the game.
# A blanket `*.COM` would be wrong: the DOS probes under tools/hwprobe are built here (and
# ignored by their own rule above).
*.EXE
*.exe
*.idata

# A raw debug/telemetry dump never belongs in the repo root, which holds only README.md,
# AGENTS.md and TODO.md. ROOT-ANCHORED on purpose, so it cannot hide a cited capture under docs/.
/*-debug.txt
